WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.310
Scale-equivariance means that when an object in an
image is resized,

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:07.732
the network's features should transform consistently,

00:00:07.812 --> 00:00:09.991
and its label should stay the same.

00:00:10.071 --> 00:00:16.641
Recent scale-equivariant convolutional networks
pursue this through weight-sharing and kernel resizing,

00:00:16.721 --> 00:00:19.739
using the same but resized kernel across scales.

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:24.323
The trouble is that these methods are derived in
the continuous domain,

00:00:24.403 --> 00:00:26.518
then discretized when implemented.

00:00:26.598 --> 00:00:31.166
That discretization step introduces a
non-negligible equivariance error,

00:00:31.246 --> 00:00:35.750
so the networks are only approximately
scale-equivariant, not truly so.
